=== 2. is Delta just length in disguise? ===
    AUC(length -> failure)          = 0.757
    AUC(q10   -> failure)           = 0.861
    AUC(q10/n -> failure)           = 0.867
    within length terciles (Delta cannot borrow length there):
      n <= 88            n= 34 unsolved= 6  AUC(q10) = 0.839   AUC(len) = 0.810
      88 < n <= 151      n= 33 unsolved=10  AUC(q10) = 0.878   AUC(len) = 0.537
      n > 151            n= 33 unsolved=20  AUC(q10) = 0.888   AUC(len) = 0.712
    likelihood-ratio test, adding q10 to a length-only model:
      LR = 28.53 on 1 df, p = 9.22e-08   beta(length) -1.85  beta(q10) +4.14

=== 3. does the slack / information-budget framing survive? ===
    slack(T) = H_avail - Delta/(RT ln2). info_budget.py frames this as the point.
    n < 150   AUC(low slack -> failure) = 0.555
    n >= 150  AUC(low slack -> failure) = 0.614
    pooled    AUC(low slack -> failure) = 0.367
    targets with NEGATIVE slack, the whole point of the framing: 0/100
    VERDICT: slack pools to 0.355 and stratifies to ~0.53-0.59, and no target ever violates
    the budget. H_avail scales with length and swamps Delta. The bits framing is dropped;
    raw Delta is the coordinate that works.

